Hello,

We appreciate your interest in participating in the Wearanize+ project. Her=
e are some documents with more information on the project as well as your r=
ights and responsibilities:
https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Snua8J5i09T8ZBXNPZGgyaoqvv0oIjxP

Please read them carefully and ask questions if you need explanations/more =
information. You must sign the Informed Consent Form at the beginning of th=
e session. You do not need to sign/send anything beforehand.

The procedure is non-invasive. Simply put, we will put some external electr=
odes on your scalp, chin, the back of your ears, and close to your eyes, tw=
o headbands on your forehead, two smartwatches on your wrists, and a small =
patch on your leg. You will then go home and sleep wearing them overnight.

Some practical information for your preparation before the session:
1. Please wear comfortable clothing (and no jewelry), something you can go =
to bed wearing.
2. If you have long hair, please tie your hair back (similar to a ponytail)=
.
3. Have an early dinner before the session.
4. Please bring a raincoat or a hooded overcoat.
5. Try to go to sleep soon after the session.

Your session will take place on [Date and Time] at EEG Lab, Trigon building=
 (address: Kapittelweg 29, 6525EN Nijmegen; nearest bus station: Nijmegen H=
AN).

We need the devices back the next morning (before noon). You can return the=
m to the Trigon building or to Building 6 of Hochschule Rhein-Waal (Kleve, =
Germany). For the sessions on Friday, you need to return the devices on Mon=
day morning.

When you arrive for the session, please wait in the waiting room (opposite =
to the reception) and let us know via email: niloy.sikder@donders.ru.nl.

Please confirm your participation as soon as possible. If you have any ques=
tions before the session, feel free to contact us as well.

With regards,
Niloy
Wearanize+ team

PS (if you are coming from Germany): You can take Bus SB58 from Emmerich/Kl=
eve/Kranenburg to reach the Trigon building. The Deutschland ticket or any =
NRW university Semester Ticket covers this travel. Please also carry your c=
redit card in case you need to travel on Dutch buses. You do not need a Dut=
ch bank account to receive the payment. Put nine zeros (000 000 000) as you=
r BSN number in the Sona system.


--_000_DB4PR10MB6192347BD877085175EAD598CBD3ADB4PR10MB6192EURP_
